    question: "What is the primary difference between a dental crown and a cap?",
    answer: "There is no clinical difference between a dental crown and a dental cap. 'Cap' is simply the familiar layperson term, while 'crown' is the professional dental term. Both refer to a custom-crafted restorative covering that completely encapsulates a damaged, root-treated, or worn tooth to restore its original shape, strength, and appearance."
  },
  {
    question: "Why is a crown strongly advised following a root canal treatment?",
    answer: "A root canal treatment removes the inflamed or infected pulp tissue from inside the tooth, which stops the blood supply to the tooth structure. Over time, the remaining tooth enamel and dentin become dehydrated and brittle. Chewing normal foods without a protective crown places extreme stress on the hollowed tooth walls, leading to vertical root fractures that often cannot be saved. A custom zirconia or ceramic crown encases the tooth and absorbs chewing forces safely."
  },
  {
    question: "How long does a monolithic zirconia or E-max crown typically last?",
    answer: "With consistent twice-daily brushing, daily flossing around the crown margins, and routine biannual checkups, monolithic zirconia and E-max lithium disilicate crowns routinely last 10 to 15 years or longer. Zirconia is exceptionally chip-resistant and withstands heavy posterior grinding pressures."
  },
  {
    question: "How much do dental crowns and caps cost in Hennur?",
    answer: "At Aureva Dental, a new patient clinical consultation including digital RVG X-ray assessment is ₹600. PFM (porcelain-fused-to-metal) crowns range from ₹4,000 to ₹6,000, all-ceramic crowns range from ₹6,000 to ₹10,000, and premium monolithic CAD/CAM Zirconia or E-max lithium disilicate crowns range from ₹10,000 to ₹18,000. Transparent written pricing is provided before any tooth preparation begins."
  },
  {
    question: "Can a chipped or broken front tooth be repaired without a full crown?",
    answer: "Yes. For minor to moderate superficial chips where the tooth pulp is unharmed, direct composite bonding (₹1,500 – ₹4,000) can restore natural contours in a single visit. However, if the fracture extends across more than half of the tooth or involves the biting edge under heavy occlusal load, a full coverage ceramic or E-max crown is recommended for long-term structural durability."
  },
  {
    question: "What is the difference between a single dental crown and a dental bridge?",
    answer: "A single crown restores an existing natural tooth that is damaged or weakened. A dental bridge replaces one or more completely missing teeth by anchoring an artificial prosthetic tooth (pontic) to the adjacent crowned natural teeth (abutments). Pricing for a dental bridge is calculated per unit, exactly matching the crown fee of the selected material."
  }
];

const breadcrumbSchema = JSON.stringify(generateBreadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbs));
const faqSchema = JSON.stringify(generateFaqSchema(faqs));
const serviceSchema = JSON.stringify(generateTreatmentServiceSchema({
  name: "Dental Crowns & Caps in Hennur",
  description: pageDescription,
  url: canonicalUrl,
  medicalSpecialty: "Prosthodontics"
}));

const seoProps = {
  title: pageTitle,
  description: pageDescription,
  canonical: canonicalUrl,
  ogTitle: pageTitle,
  ogDescription: pageDescription,
  ogUrl: canonicalUrl,
  schemaMarkup: [breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema, serviceSchema]
