          Dental Bridges for Missing Teeth: Per-Unit Precision
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          When one or two consecutive teeth are missing, a fixed dental bridge offers a stable, non-removable restorative option without needing surgical implant placement. A bridge consists of two anchoring crowns placed over the natural teeth on either side of the space (abutments), connected to an artificial suspended prosthetic tooth in the middle (pontic).
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          At Aureva Dental, pricing for dental bridges is completely straightforward: it is calculated per unit, exactly matching the individual crown price of your chosen material. For instance, a 3-unit monolithic zirconia bridge replacing one missing molar consists of 3 crown units (₹10,000 – ₹18,000 per unit). Our clinicians verify perfect bite balance and seamless margin adaptation using digital RVG imaging so your bridge feels natural from day one.
        </p>
